                                          <h1 class="small-text-size-four-xl text-size-three-xl font-powerhouse title-font text-yellow-five-hundred">A Thoughtful Approach to Interior Design</h1>
                                          <p class="large-width-two-thirds-path margin-x-auto-path line-height-relaxation text-size-base-casting text-gray-nine-hundred">
                                                 Good interior design balances atmosphere with practical use. North Room Atelier takes time to understand how a room needs to function, what its existing features contribute, and which changes matter most to you. Design ideas are developed with attention to proportion, light, colour, materials, and furnishings, so that individual choices support a coherent whole. The process is collaborative rather than one-size-fits-all: priorities and scope are
                                                 discussed together, and the direction can be reviewed as the project develops.
                                          </p>
                                   </div>
                                   <div class="large-width-two-thirds-path margin-x-auto-path">
                                          <div class="flex-fusion flex-wrap-journey negative-margin-four">
                                                 <div class="padding-four-space large-width-half-bridge medium-width-full-scope">
                                                        <div class="flex-fusion border-two-boundary border-gray-seven-hundred rounded-large-crest padding-eight-crest flex-column-path background-gray-six-hundred">
                                                               <h2 class="text-size-xl-vibe font-middle-ground text-yellow-five-hundred margin-bottom-two-space">Designed Around Your Brief</h2>
                                                               <p class="text-size-large-canvas line-height-relaxation text-gray-three-hundred">
                                                                      Each project begins with your needs, preferences, and the way you use your space. A conversation about routines, priorities, existing furnishings, and desired atmosphere helps establish a useful design brief before ideas are developed. This keeps the work connected to your home rather than relying on a fixed style or a predetermined solution. The brief also gives you a shared reference point for discussing choices, clarifying
                                                                      what is in scope, and deciding which design questions need attention first.
                                                               </p>
                                                        </div>
                                                 </div>
                                                 <div class="padding-four-space large-width-half-bridge medium-width-full-scope">
                                                        <div class="flex-fusion border-two-boundary border-gray-seven-hundred rounded-large-crest padding-eight-crest flex-column-path background-gray-six-hundred">
                                                               <h2 class="text-size-xl-vibe font-middle-ground text-yellow-five-hundred margin-bottom-two-space">Connected Design Decisions</h2>
                                                               <p class="text-size-large-canvas line-height-relaxation text-gray-three-hundred">
                                                                      A room feels considered when its individual elements work together. North Room Atelier explores how layout, colour, materials, lighting, and furnishings relate to one another, while also respecting the character and constraints of the property. Rather than treating each choice in isolation, the design process considers the overall balance of the interior and the experience of moving through it. This joined-up thinking can help
                                                                      you assess options more clearly and shape a direction that feels consistent with your brief.
                                                               </p>
                                                        </div>
                                                 </div>
                                                 <div class="padding-four-space large-width-half-bridge medium-width-full-scope margin-top-four-fleece">
                                                        <div class="flex-fusion border-two-boundary border-gray-seven-hundred rounded-large-crest padding-eight-crest flex-column-path background-gray-six-hundred">
                                                               <h2 class="text-size-xl-vibe font-middle-ground text-yellow-five-hundred margin-bottom-two-space">Practicality Alongside Atmosphere</h2>
                                                               <p class="text-size-large-canvas line-height-relaxation text-gray-three-hundred">
                                                                      An interior should feel inviting, but it also needs to support everyday life. Design discussions can consider circulation, storage needs, how rooms are used, and the practical qualities of proposed materials and furnishings. These considerations sit alongside colour, texture, lighting, and visual character, rather than being left until the end. By keeping function and atmosphere in view together, the design can respond to the
                                                                      realities of your home as well as the mood you would like each space to convey.
                                                               </p>
                                                        </div>
                                                 </div>
                                                 <div class="padding-four-space large-width-half-bridge medium-width-full-scope margin-top-four-fleece">
                                                        <div class="flex-fusion border-two-boundary border-gray-seven-hundred rounded-large-crest padding-eight-crest flex-column-path background-gray-six-hundred">
                                                               <h2 class="text-size-xl-vibe font-middle-ground text-yellow-five-hundred margin-bottom-two-space">A Clear, Collaborative Process</h2>
                                                               <p class="text-size-large-canvas line-height-relaxation text-gray-three-hundred">
                                                                      A considered process makes it easier to understand how a design develops and where your input is needed. North Room Atelier discusses the project brief, scope, and preferred direction with you, then uses those conversations to guide design decisions and subsequent refinement. Questions and feedback are part of the work, not an interruption to it. The exact stages, deliverables, timing, and fees depend on the project and are
                                                                      clarified individually, so expectations can be discussed before you decide how to proceed.
                                                               </p>
